s Enfants","dish/au-coin-des-bons-enfants"],["Au Crocodile","dish/au-crocodile"],["Au Pied de Cochon (Mexico City)","dish/au-pied-de-cochon-mexico-city"],["Auberge (restaurant)","dish/auberge-restaurant"],["Auberge De Kieviet","dish/auberge-de-kieviet"],["Aubergine (London restaurant)","dish/aubergine-london-restaurant"],["Auguste (restaurant)","dish/auguste-restaurant"],["Bagatelle (restaurant)","dish/bagatelle-restaurant"],["Balthazar (restaurant)","dish/balthazar-restaurant"],["Bardot Brasserie","dish/bardot-brasserie"],["Bâtard (restaurant)","dish/batard-restaurant"],["Baumé (restaurant)","dish/baume-restaurant"],["Bayonne ham","dish/bayonne-ham"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beaulieu, Doorwerth Castle","dish/beaulieu-doorwerth-castle"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Bell's (restaurant)","dish/bell-s-restaurant"],["Belmond Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons","dish/belmond-le-manoir-aux-quat-saisons"],["Beluga (restaurant)","dish/beluga-restaurant"],["Berowra Waters Inn","dish/berowra-waters-inn"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Bistro 990","dish/bistro-990"],["Bistro Agnes","dish/bistro-agnes"],["Bistro Jeanty","dish/bistro-jeanty"]]}]},"dish/rak":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rak","n":"Rakı","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Turkish cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Rakı is an alcoholic beverage made of twice-distilled grape pomace and flavored with aniseed. It is a national drink of Turkey, and it is especially popular in the coastal regions. Among drinkers of alcoholic beverages, it is popular in Turkic countries and Caucasian countries as an apéritif. It is often served with seafood or meze. It is comparable to several other anise-flavored liqueurs such as pastis, ouzo, sambuca and arak. The alcoholic content of rakı must be at least 40% according to Turkish standard. The largest producer of raki is Diageo, which operates in Turkey through its subsidiary Mey İçki (acquired in 2011); Yeni Rakı is the largest brand. Rakı has been a registered geographical indication in Turkey since 2009, granting it legal protection as a spirit produced exclusively from Turkish-grown grapes and anise."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rak"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rak%C4%B1"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Barrel","ingredient/barrel"],["Date","ingredient/date"],["Fig","ingredient/fig"],["Grape","ingredient/grape"],["Pomace","ingredient/pomace"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","ref":"site/ozlemsturkishtable-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Turkish cuisine","links":[["Adana kebabı","dish/adana-kebab"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bici bici","dish/bici-bici"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Çiğ köfte","dish/cig-kofte"],["Çökertme kebabı","dish/cokertme-kebab"],["Dede (restaurant)","dish/dede-restaurant"],["Doner kebab","dish/doner-kebab"],["Düğün çorbası","dish/dugun-corbas"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["İskender kebap","dish/iskender-kebap"],["Kavurma","dish/kavurma"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Kuru fasulye","dish/kuru-fasulye"],["Kyopolou","dish/kyopolou"],["Mesir macunu","dish/mesir-macunu"],["Nevzine tatlısı","dish/nevzine-tatl-s"],["Ntolmás","dish/ntolmas"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Piyaz","dish/piyaz"],["Qatlama","dish/qatlama"],["Şıllık","dish/s-ll-k"],["Sofra (restaurant)","dish/sofra-restaurant"],["Stuffed leaves","dish/stuffed-leaves"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"],["Stuffed tomatoes","dish/stuffed-tomatoes"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Yayla çorbası","dish/yayla-corbas"]]}]},"dish/ribollita":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ribollita","n":"Ribollita","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Tuscan cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Ribollita is a Tuscan panade (a variety of bread soup) made with bread and vegetables, often from leftovers. There are many variations, but it usually contains cannellini beans, lacinato kale, cabbage and inexpensive vegetables such as carrot, beans, chard, celery, potatoes and onion. It is often baked in a clay pot."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ribollita"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribollita"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Tuscan cuisine","cuisine/tuscan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Brassica oleracea var. palmifolia","ingredient/brassica-oleracea-var-palmifolia"],["Kidney bean","ingredient/kidney-bean"],["Phaseolus vulgaris","ingredient/phaseolus-vulgaris"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Juls' Kitchen","ref":"site/en-julskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"en.julskitchen.com","note":"Tuscan cook and author Giulia Scarpaleggia's blog of Tuscan home recipes.","url":"https://en.julskitchen.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Divina Cucina","ref":"site/divinacucina-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"divinacucina.com","note":"Florence-based cooking teacher Judy Witts Francini's site on Tuscan food.","url":"https://divinacucina.com/?p=3266","suggested":true}]}]},"ingredient/shark-s-fin":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/shark-s-fin","n":"Shark's fin","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Shark fin soup is a soup or stewed dish served in parts of China, Taiwan, and Southeast Asia. The shark fins provide texture, while the taste comes from the other ingredients. As one of the four sea delicacies, it is commonly served at special occasions such as weddings and banquets, or as a luxury item."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-shark-s-fin"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark's_fin"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Shark fin soup","dish/shark-fin-soup"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Shark meat","ingredient/shark-meat"]]}]},"dish/weckewerk":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/weckewerk","n":"Weckewerk","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Hessian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Weckewerk is a sausage, native to Northern Hesse, Germany. It is made from cooked brawn and minced meat, veal or sausage, and broth of pork, sometimes from cooked meat, blood and offal. The sausage is stretched with stale bread, explaining the name: \"Weck\" or \"Wegge\" is the traditional term for roll in Northern Hesse. It is seasoned with onions, salt, pepper, marjoram, regionally also with caraway, allspice and garlic. The ingredients are ground and mixed. To be consumed within a short time, the mixture is packaged in pig intestines. If longer storage is desired, it is preserved in jars or filled in artificial casings."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-weckewerk"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weckewerk"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Hessian cuisine","cuisine/hessian-cuisine"]]}]},"cookbook/cook-korean":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/cook-korean","n":"Cook Korean!","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Robin Ha, 2016","square":true,"suggested":true,"isbn":"9781607748878","intro":[["Korean recipes presented as illustrated comics by a Korean-born cartoonist."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252746/cook-korean-by-robin-ha/9781607748878/","label":"Publisher or book page"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"]]}]},"site/princesstafadzwa-com":{"t":"site","r":"site/princesstafadzwa-com","n":"Princess Tafadzwa","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Recipe sites","sites"]],"sub":"Recipe site, princesstafadzwa.com","square":true,"suggested":true,"intro":[["Zimbabwean recipes using Shona ingredients and dish names, alongside craft posts."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://princesstafadzwa.com","label":"Visit princesstafadzwa.com"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Zimbabwean cuisine","ref":"cuisine/zimbabwean-cuisine","color":"#e46a3f","shape":"cuisine","sub":"Princess Tafadzwa","url":"https://www.princesstafadzwa.com/"}]}]}}